    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so im working with a client who's pretty much stuck on their squat. been at the same weight for like 3 weeks now and they cant seem to move past it. can u explain how doing a deload week or messing with the volume might actually help them break through that plateau?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely. A deload week involves reducing the intensity and volume of your workout, which allows your muscles to recover and adapt, potentially increasing strength. Frequently hitting a plateau can lead to overtraining, where fatigue and inadequate recovery inhibit progress. By incorporating a deload week, your client's muscles can fully recover, and the reduced volume may also provide a different stimulus, promoting strength gains. After this period, they can resume their normal routine and might notice improved performance.",
